Subject: [PATCH 07/10] lakeside olive (r5h3 alignment): far hills, terrain
 grass and far-shore grass on their own olive palette cells

Grok Bot approved; aligns with Funning's chosen r5h3 (no new art direction). Vertex colours cannot do it (COLOR_0 only
multiplies: the far hills' red would need ~x6 linear), so the palette path, isolated:
- T_LK_palette_256.png: 6 new cells in the free row 10 (all black before, sampled by no GLB): hills 4fa0a0 -> 93a77c,
  2f6446 -> 5b6835, 3f7f52 -> 77853e, 5a93a8 -> a69982; grass 6dbe45 -> 398f12, a8d64a -> 5ca214. Shared cells unchanged,
  PNG stays RGB with its sRGB/gAMA/cHRM chunks (1,803 -> 1,007 B, IDAT re-encoded).
- LK_far_hills.glb (1,491 UVs), LK_terrain.glb (994), LK_far_shore.glb (656): float32 TEXCOORD_0 moved to those cells in
  place; byte sizes, vertex counts, COLOR_0, image and material unchanged -> static merge / instancing unchanged, 0 added
  draws, the journey loads the same assets (no pop). Grass tufts, bushes, trees and all 45 other GLBs untouched.
- tools/lakeside/olive_recolour.py (idempotent; re-run after any .blend re-export), guard test lakeside-olive.
Stand-in emulator (f7f892f lights, board camera): far hills 26/78/30 -> 71/84/20 (r5h3 far region 71/83/20); far_trees
region 29/94/30 -> 51/94/28 (the far trees stay green: shared tree GLBs not changed); grass_L 109/134/59 -> 87/107/45
(r5h3 81/107/24); grass_R 114/138/61 -> 93/111/48 (72/120/22).
